hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1455.1","Malik related to me from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"1455.2","Malik related to me from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"1456.1","Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm that Amr ibn Sulaym az-Zuraqi informed his father that it had been said to Umar ibn al-Khattab"
"1456.2","Malik related to me from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Hazm that Amr ibn Sulaym az-Zuraqi informed his father that it had been said to Umar ibn al-Khattab"
"1457.1","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Abu Bakr ibn Hazm that a boy from Ghassan was dying in Madina while his heir was in Syria. That was mentioned to Umar ibn al-Khattab. It was said to him"
"1457.2","Malik related to me from Yahya ibn Said from Abu Bakr ibn Hazm that a boy from Ghassan was dying in Madina while his heir was in Syria. That was mentioned to Umar ibn al-Khattab. It was said to him"
"1458.1","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab from Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas that his father said"
"1458.2","Malik related to me from Ibn Shihab from Amir ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas that his father said"
"1459.1","Malik narrated to me, from Rabi'ah bin Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Yazid, the freed slave of al-M"
"1459.2","Mālik narrated to me, from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Yazīd, the freed slave of al-Munbaʿith, from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, that he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and asked him about found property. He said: \"Identify its container and its tie, then announce it for a year. If its owner comes, otherwise, do as you please with it.\" He said: \"And what about a lost sheep, O Messenger of Allāh?\" He said: \"It is for you, or for your brother, or for the wolf.\" He said: \"And what about a lost camel?\" He said: \"What concern do you have with it? It has its water and its pasture; it drinks from the water and eats from the trees until its owner finds it.\""
"1460.1","Malik related to me that Yahya ibn Said said that he heard al- Qasim ibn Muhammad say"
"1460.2","Malik related to me that Yahya ibn Said said that he heard al- Qasim ibn Muhammad say"
"1461.1","Yahya said that he heard Malik speak about a man who bought goods - animals or clothes or wares"
"1461.2","Yahya said that he heard Malik speak about a man who bought goods - animals or clothes or wares"
"1462.1","Malik related to me from Umar ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Dalaf al- Muzani from his father that a man from the Juhayna tribe used to buy camels before people set out for hajj and sell them at a higher price. Then he travelled quickly and used to arrive in Makka before the others who set out for hajj. He went bankrupt and his situation was put before Umar ibn al-Khattab"
"1462.2","Malik related to me from Umar ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Dalaf al- Muzani from his father that a man from the Juhayna tribe used to buy camels before people set out for hajj and sell them at a higher price. Then he travelled quickly and used to arrive in Makka before the others who set out for hajj. He went bankrupt and his situation was put before Umar ibn al-Khattab"
"1463.1","Mālik narrated to me, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that ʿUmar"
"1463.2","Mālik narrated to me, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb said, while leaning his back against the Kaʿbah: \"Whoever takes a lost animal is himself lost.\""
